note Word access for the aligned paths. b8 is the caller's 8-byte-aligned copy of the input lent a
note second time as ulong cells (b views the same bytes), so one load brings 8 bytes. Swapping the
note bytes inside each 32-bit half (two mask-and-shift steps; the constants stay in registers) turns
note little-endian bytes b0..b7 into the big-endian words b0..b3 (low half) and b4..b7 (high half).
note Each word is stored duplicated, as expand requires.
fn blk8 b8 view ulong 512 q ulong w edit ulong 64 to void
for i ulong 8
x = get b8 add q i
y = or shl and x 71777214294589695 8 and shr x 8 71777214294589695
y = or shl and y 281470681808895 16 and shr y 16 281470681808895
j = mul i 2
t = shl y 32
put w j or t shr t 32
put w add j 1 or and y 18446744069414584320 shr y 32
end
end

note the padded tail b[off..n) (less than 64 bytes), read as words through b8 (the bytes past n
note are inside the caller's 4096-byte copy and are masked off here): the word holding byte n keeps
note its k valid bytes and gets 0x80 after them, later words are zero, the 64-bit bit count goes in
note words 14 and 15; a second block when the tail is 56 bytes or more
fn tail8 h edit uint 8 b8 view ulong 512 off ulong n ulong w edit ulong 64 to void
blk8 b8 shr off 3 w
r = sub n off
fw = shr r 2
k = and r 3
sh = mul k 8
v = get w fw
v = and v shl 4294967295 sub 32 sh
v = and v 4294967295
v = or v shl 128 sub 24 sh
put w fw or v shl v 32
i = add fw 1
while lt i 16 bound 16
put w i 0
i = add i 1
end
if ge r 56
expand w
rounds h w
for j ulong 14
put w j 0
end
end
bits = mul n 8
v = shr bits 32
put w 14 or v shl v 32
v = and bits 4294967295
put w 15 or v shl v 32
expand w
rounds h w
end

note the digest of h as 32 bytes packed little endian into w[0..4): word i holds the big-endian
note bytes of h[2i] then h[2i+1], so the caller copies the digest out of w with memcpy
fn digest8 h edit uint 8 w edit ulong 64 to void
for i ulong 4
j = mul i 2
x = or ulong get h j shl ulong get h add j 1 32
y = or shl and x 71777214294589695 8 and shr x 8 71777214294589695
y = or shl and y 281470681808895 16 and shr y 16 281470681808895
put w i y
end
end

note SHA-256 of the n < 4096 bytes in b8, state in locals only (sha256_hash's short path)
fn oneshot b8 view ulong 512 n ulong w edit ulong 64 to void
if ge n 4096
trap 3
end
h = new uint 8 0
initiv h
off = ulong 0
while le add off 64 n bound 64
blk8 b8 shr off 3 w
expand w
rounds h w
off = add off 64
end
tail8 h b8 off n w
digest8 h w
end

fn omsha c edit uchar 104 b view uchar 4096 n ulong op ulong w edit ulong 64 b8 view ulong 512 to void
if eq op 0
init c
ret
end
if eq op 1
absorb c b n w
ret
end
if eq op 2
final c w
ret
end
if eq op 3
oneshot b8 n w
ret
end
trap 9
end
